{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "auth-collection-id",
		"name": "Nuvana Authentication API",
		"description": "## Nuvana Authentication API Collection\n\nThis collection contains all authentication-related endpoints for the Nuvana system, supporting multiple roles: Super Admin, School Admin, Teacher, and Student.\n\n### How Tokens Work\n\n1. **Access Token**: A short-lived JWT token used to authenticate most API requests. It should be sent in the `Authorization` header as a Bearer token: \n   `Authorization: Bearer <your_access_token>`\n\n2. **Refresh Token**: A long-lived JWT token used to obtain a new access token when the current one expires. It is sent to the `/auth/refresh` endpoint.\n\n### Authentication Flow\n\n1. **Login**: Perform a login request with your credentials and `expectedRole` (optional but recommended).\n2. **Store Tokens**: Upon successful login, you will receive an `access_token` and a `refresh_token`.\n3. **Authorize Requests**: Use the `access_token` for all subsequent requests requiring authentication.\n4. **Handle Expiry**: If a request returns a `401 Unauthorized` error, use the `refresh_token` to get a new `access_token`.\n\n### Roles in Nuvana\n\n| Role | ID | Description |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| `super_admin` | 1 | Full system access, manages schools |\n| `school_admin` | 2 | Manages school-specific settings and users |\n| `teacher` | 3 | Manages classes, attendance, and content |\n| `student` | 4 | Accesses courses, quizzes, and learning materials |\n\n### Base URL\n\nThe default base URL is `http://localhost:3000`. You can change this using Postman environments.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
